   "text": {
    "L1": "In a letter puzzle, the same letter always means the same digit.",
    "L2": "Different letters mean different digits, and a leading digit cannot be zero.",
    "L3": "We solve from the ones column first, and we keep every carry.",
    "L4": "For A5 plus 1A equals 92, the ones say 5 plus A ends in 2.",
    "L5": "So 5 plus A is 12, not 2. That makes A equal to 7, with a carry of 1.",
    "L6": "Now check the tens: 7 plus 1 plus the carry 1 equals 9.",
    "L7": "The myth is wrong: solving columns alone can miss the carry into the next column.",
    "L8": "So 75 plus 17 equals 92. What should we inspect first?"
   },
